# flOW — application module contract.
#
# A module is a self-contained slice of the app, managed by the App at runtime
# (parameterizable via config, enable/disable, reload). Implement these methods:
#
#   name()                 -> string (unique module id, e.g. "sound")
#   requires()             -> array of service names this module depends on
#   register(app)          -> wire up: provide services, read config
#   start(app)             -> run: emit events, use resolved services
#   on_event(type, payload)-> react to events (no-op if not interested)
#   reload(app)            -> reset this module's state (no-op if stateless)
#
# The App delivers every emitted event to each ENABLED module's on_event, so
# modules stay decoupled — a publisher never references its subscribers.
interface Module:
  fn name()
  fn requires()
  fn register(app)
  fn start(app)
  fn on_event(type, payload)
  fn reload(app)
